Movies flashed the last gameplay frame (or black) between their pictures. The USA movie player draws every picture
into fbp 104, a buffer whose memory covers fbp 208, and flips DISPFB between 104 and 208; Present showed the 208 target,
which still held the last gameplay frame (or did not exist). Present now shows the newest target drawn over the displayed
buffer's first block when the displayed target itself was not drawn during the last 16 presents (~0.27 s) and that
newer target was. Gameplay redraws its displayed buffer every one or two presents, so the rule does not apply there
(a first draft using a one-present gap also fired in sub-60 FPS gameplay, where 104 holds an intermediate pass).
Logs one [gs-hw-display] line per ~5 s window in which it applied.

